          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f726fa1fb17b2ff1c977d146c3fb2b807532f9c94fcf57edeb416b7b737eb19:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b387d54901e5425a84b4220ffcb1a549",
      "statement": "`tabId` travels on the protocol envelope's `target.tabId` and the relay forwards the whole envelope unchanged; `BrijioBackgroundController.handleSocketMessage` calls `extractTabId(message)` to read `message.target.tabId`, validate it as a non-empty string, parse it to a number, and forward that numeric `tabId` into each handler and adapter call (page context/content, action, batch, navigation, open-tab, screenshot). When `tabId` is absent the controller passes `undefined`, which each shared helper resolves to the active foreground tab.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0062-thread-tabid-through-action-stack.md#L60-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0f2973329f226c1fccd40e4b75ba88ca2433ecfa32f3dc190cf13275b44bb77:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/background-controller.ts#L564-L655",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7611e5033a089dce6406690136731adff7487cea40c3fbb71047a2d198eed02:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7071c501fbce40328d645d7cf664aeca",
      "statement": "The active-tab fallback is a preserved, backward-compatible invariant: on the MCP side `page-actions.ts` builds every `request*` options object with `tabId: tabId ?? config.defaultTabId`, and on the extension side `page-reader.ts`'s `readActiveTabPage` uses the numeric `tabId` directly as `resolvedTabId` for `scripting.executeScript`/`tabs.sendMessage` when present and otherwise falls back to `deps.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true })`. A tool that should work on a background tab must accept `tabId` and must not assume the active tab.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0060-explicit-tab-listing-and-selection.md#L24-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ac359fcc39609f59482552f53c4740c9102eb34a38bd2aaf59e90b59e8d601b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/page-reader.ts#L118-L145",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0dfe78d1704ccfb3c1485190594fde8cab0af62529faa1771ad96e5c0a97f836:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/page-actions.ts#L115-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30c51c5a9df0517703f781a595c96182f4bf3ff364be5613bf7ad40dc6e31320:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13b6f02d0f33426c93f9beeb328387c0",
      "statement": "`navigate_to_url` and `perform_batch` are currently tabId-wiring gaps: both declare `tabId` in their tool input, but `navigate-to-url-tool.ts` calls `navigateToCurrentPageUrl(config, url, browserInstanceId)` without the `tabId` argument, and `batch-tool.ts`'s `performBatchTool` passes only `browserInstanceId`, `continueOnError`, `readAfterActions`, `pageContextId`, `visibleContextId` into `performBatch` — never `input.tabId`. The underlying `page-actions.ts` `navigateToCurrentPageUrl`/`performBatch` accept and forward `tabId` (`tabId: tabId ?? config.defaultTabId` / `tabId: options?.tabId ?? config.defaultTabId`), so the gap is in the tool-module wiring, not the action layer, and passing `tabId` to either tool silently falls back to the active tab.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/batch-tool.ts#L93-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f0200b0b520147762f5b429a1255ea8cbf5321c783627c7c845c1a461af2a4f:"
        },
        {
